    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d954">

                <pb facs="1075" n="931" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg931"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.8312 A/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-17T18:00:00-04:00">August 17, 1928—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>27. On August 16th the Secretary handed to the Attaché of the Egyptian Legation a
                        note<anchor n="1" xml:id="d954-f1"/> proposing the negotiation of treaties
                    of arbitration and conciliation between the United States and Egypt. The note
                    was accompanied by draft texts in all respects similar to those which have been
                    proposed during recent months to other countries. Arbitration treaties have been
                    proposed to 29 other countries and signed with 8. Conciliation treaties have
                    been proposed to 19 other countries and signed with 5.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
